jknights@qc.bell.ca (James Knights) writes:

>I have 2 RZ55-FA SCSI disks. They were bought to be used with VAXstation
>3100s, but never used (they may not even be formatted).

>I want to use them with an Mac 660 AV. I attach the cables, verify that
>the terminator is on, the SCSI address, etc. When I use SCSI Probe, it
>has no problem seeing the disk. When I try to format it (I have tried 3
>different formatting programs), I get the message 'Error 03 -
>drive not ready'. 

Ah, you hit the famous spinup problem. If I'm correctr, the RZ55
come configured to spinup only after they receive a spinup from the
host. This is done to avoid big inrush currents when all disks spinup
at the same time.

I don't know about the vax, but for for Ultrix there is a utility
called rzdisk, and for OSF/1 there is 'scu' that lets you change
the drives spinup behaviour.

Wilko
