        Short answer: The disk LD_TSB3 is so fragmented, and/or there
    	              are so many files on the disk, that               
                      [000000]INDEXF.SYS can't be extended any more.  
                      Do an image BACKUP and restore of the disk.     

        Long answer:  Look up the recent archives of comp.os.vms.  
    		      There was a long thread there about file header
    		      full messages, INDEXF.SYS and its extents, and
    		      how to pre-extend INDEXF.SYS so that the same
    		      problem doesn't recur, at least not too soon...

