>$ copy sys$login:login.com []/log
>%COPY-E-OPENOUT, error opening LD_TSB2:[TSBVI_COMMON]LOGIN.COM;83 as output
>-RMS-E-CRE, ACP file create failed
>-SYSTEM-W-HEADERFULL, file header is full

To recover from this error, there's only one method: restore an image backup.
To prevent: use an disk defragmentation tool, or do a regular image restore.
To monitor it: make an dump of the indexf.sys, and look in the first pages for
the string 'map area words'. The figure behind it tells you the level of which
the table header is filled. 140-150 is an almost full header. Usually it should be 
lower then 120.

Greetings,

Marc

