>	I just recently got a Microvax III+ and have been busy trying to
>swap hardware around between it and my Vaxstation II.  The fun of it all comes
>down to me trying to put three different tape drives on this thing.  I'm
>not sure if it's possible to get three controllers to work or not...but here's
>what I've got and what I've tried.

>	TQK70 (TK70 controller) at the primary CSR address.
>	TQK50 (TK50 controller) at the secondary CSR address 760404.
>	EMULEX QT13 (Pertec interface) at CSR address 760444.

>	When I try this, the TK70 comes up a MUA0, the TK50 I think as
>	MUB0, and the third doesn't come up at all.  I tried to pull a fast
>	one by running SYSGEN and using the CONNECT command for MUC0 using
>	the above CSR and the system decided to reboot. :( 

>	Any suggestions of how to make this thing work, that is - if it's
>	possible?  If so, if using CONNECT happens to be a step in the right
>	direction, I may need help on the syntax.

One of the nice things of an uVaxIII is that it has a console command,
config, which will take as input all the devices you plan on having on
your system and producing an address/vector table for them.  I would
suggest you do this with your system, then you're sure to have things
set a (mostly) reasonable way.

When you are entering devices and have one which is non-digital, simply
enter the digital device it resembles.

