where one bus is reserved for async i/o (tape,CD), one for the system disk
and the other 4 channels for 2 sets of shadowed stripesets (see below).

                                         XMI
        -----+-----------------+-----------------+------
             !                 !                 !
        +----+----+      +-----+-----+    +------+-----+
        !         !      !           !    !            !
        ! A    B  !      !  C     D  !    !   E     F  !
        +---------+      +-----------+    +------------+
          !    !            !     !           !     !
         tape boot          !     !           !     !
          cd              rz28  rz28        rz28   rz28
                           x5    x5          x5     x5


Our plans are to stripe entire channels (make all devices on bus C one
stripeset, all on E another stripeset) and then shadow device zero on
channel C to device 0 on channel E. Same for channels D and F. This seems
to give both maximum i/o distribution and security. Is there something I
have forgot ?

