This is the first in a series of free bi-monthly Electronic-Mail Newsletters
from Parallel Performance Group of Sedona, Arizona, on Project Management
software tools in general, as well as specific state-of-the-art Project
Management software products.

The Newsletter will cover Gantt Charts, the rationale and theory behind the
Critcal Path and PERT network models in Project Management, and survey the
various ways these are used and the reports and other tools based on them.
Later issues will cover Software Configuration Management.

Parallel Performance Group specializes in the marketing and distribution of
high-technology scientific and engineering software, principally to users of
engineering-type computer workstations and software practitioners.  Through
this Newsletter, we hope to provide software practitioners and Project Managers
with a more-than-casual insight into Project Management by presenting a survey
of the state-of-the-art and tutorial examples of various applications.


                              ACCENT GraphicVUE

ACCENT GraphicVUE is a powerful and flexible project management package for
use on UNIX workstations.  It is also the first "mainframe class" system to
support OSF/Motif as well as OPEN LOOK.  It employs mouse-driven windows,
pull-down menus, point-and-click actions, drag actions, and toolbar buttons
that greatly simplify the interactions for project definition and management.
ACCENT GraphicVUE operates on Sun SparcStations, and HP Apollo, IBM RS/6000,
DEC Alpha, and Silicon Graphics Workstations, as well as PC's running SCO Unix.

ACCENT GraphicVUE provides two interchangeable views of a project for data
entry or analysis. The default view is a split-screen Gantt/Spreadsheet main
window that allows pictorial manipulation of the Gantt chart and/or data
entry in the spreadsheet. The boundary can be moved to expand either the
Gantt chart or the spreadsheet, as needed.

With the click of a toolbar button the main window can be converted to a PERT
network view of the project.  The user can now perform pictorial manipulations
on the PERT chart along with a new set of pull-down menus and toolbar buttons
for that environment.  A Global View subwindow can be opened within the main
window to provide an overall view and facilitate movement to other parts of the
PERT network.  GraphicVUE tracks over 40 separate types of data for each acti-
vity/task. 

GraphicVUE does all date calculations and automatically tracks and totals
project cost estimates and resource utilizations, activity-by-activity and
project-by-project.  A Resource Histogram can be invoked to apply (specify)
or level (redistribute) resources.  Up to 30 different 20-year calendars can
be specified to support even the most unusual work schedules.  The Critical
(longest) Path is automatically calculated and continuously highlighted.

Projects scattered across a workstation network can be included in multi-
project processing. Project information can be combined and distributed
across directories, networks, and geographical sites to facilitate distributed
project planning and control.  The Project Manager can choose from over 50
standard reports. Subwindows provide options for selection, sorting, and for-
matting reports to show only the information needed. All reports can be pre-
viewed on-screen.

ACCENT GraphicVUE software is accompanied by clear documentation that includes
an Installation Guide, a very comprehensive tutorial Self-Guided Tour, and a
User's Manual that will help the experienced Project Manager as well as the
first-time user of project management tools.

Our next issue will introduce the Gantt Chart and Critical Path Method (CPM)
and PERT network models of Project Management Scheduling, and discuss the
connections among networks, CPM, and Linear Programming..

