>to do something at the console level to tell the 6310 that he has more
>memory?? 
>

Did you run AUTOGEN?  If you've run AUTOGEN before on your V6.0 system, it set
the SYSGEN parameter PHYSICALPAGES to be 32MB (64k pages) for you.  If you run
AUTOGEN again with the larger memory, it'll pick up the fact that you now have
64MB memory and re-do things so that the 64MB will work.  Of course, you'll
need to reboot after the AUTOGEN run.


