The RZ23 has no jumpers, ;-(, also the RZ22,RZ24,RZ55,RZ56.

>Does anyone out there know if there is a jumper on the drive which will make
>it spin up when it gets power.  I called connor, who makes the drive, they 
>would not help.  I also called dec and they wanted to charge me some ridiculous
>fees for tech support.  Please e-mail me a response since I do not usually 
>read this news group.

But if you have a mv3100 there is hope.

	1. install an mmj loopback connector in the system com port.
	2. Disconnect any RX23 from the system
	3. install the 'victom' drive.
	4. power up the system and run diag t73
	>>> T 73 <ret>

  KA42-A TPmker
						   
  VStmk_QUE_id (0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7) ? 0 <----Enter ID address of drive
							    
  VStmk_QUE_RUsure (1/0) ?   <----Enter 42000001 ( to ENABLE spin up bit)
								     
     or
                             <-----Enter 41000001 ( to DISABLE spin up bit)

        5. The test will complain about an error, saying that the 'victom' is
	   not an tape drive ;-), that we must take as being a correct 
	   statement.

	6. power off the machine, disconnect the the scsi-cable, power up the
	   machine again and it must spinup now.

p.s. This diag is only availible on Mvax3100 not on RISC as far as i known,
     have fun with the new autospinup noisy RZ-drive.


