According to the catalog, there is 8MB of memory embedded on the system board,
and you can add up to 2 16MB memory options for a total of 40MB of memory. 
You're dealer appears to be correct, unless someone else has larger memory
SIMMs available.  I don't know of any, however.

>2. Is it poosible for us to upgrade our DS5000/25 into one with a
>   CPU faster than what we currently have?

According to the catalog, there is a KN02-DC upgrade kit to make it a 33Mhz
cpu, instead of your 25Mhz cpu.  This will give you about a 33% increase in cpu
speed (based on a quick calculation of the clock speeds, only).  

There is also the PM40U-AA option to upgrade you to the R4000 cpu.  I believe
this cpu runs at 50Mhz.

>3. Will ULTRIX V4.4 solve the above problems?

What problem?  The thrashing?  Probably not.  If you're out of memory, you're
out of memory.

