In article <Conu7z.31@kddlab.kddlabs.co.jp>, tru@kddnews.kddlabs.co.jp (Tohru Asami) writes:

>The dealer of this machine said that we cannot increase the memory
>over 40MB.
>
>If you know something about the following questions, please let me know.
>
>1. Is there any way to increase a phisical memory size of this machine?

Doesn't appear to be.  According to the November 1992 System and
Options Catalog the Personal DECstation has four memory slots.
Since the MS01-CA 16 MB SIMM is used to get to 40 MB and this
is the maximum support by the system (2 and a fraction SIMMs)
the limit must be enforced by the hardware.  A rather odd limit
but there was probably a reason at the time.

>2. Is it poosible for us to upgrade our DS5000/25 into one with a
>   CPU faster than what we currently have?

Maybe.  There was an R4000 upgrade available for the Personal
DECstation, which may still be available.  Contact a DEC sales
person.

>3. Will ULTRIX V4.4 solve the above problems?

The 40 MB limit has nearly got to be hardware and a different
version of the OS won't change it.  ULTRIX V4.4 would be the
appropriate version for supporting the CPU upgrade.  The
only ways I see to solve the memory problem are:

o  Find a different model DECstation that supports more
   memory.  A Model 100 or 240 would be good choices.

o  Upgrade to an AXP system.
