In article <19APR199409282317@uhcl2>, csci2424@uhcl2 (Tim Dugan) writes:

|>Can someone please help me...  I have the Dec DECTALK
|>system, but the only documentation I have is an installation
|>guide.  Can someone tell me where to get the rest on-line?

   You don't mention the host operating system in use, nor the
   particular model of DECtalk -- the following are general
   answers.

   There is no online documentation for the DECtalk DTC01 or
   DTC03 devices.  (Even engineers from Digital's Voice Products
   Group worked from the hardcopy documentation when working with
   those devices.)

   One needs to order the owner's manual for the appropriate
   model of DECtalk -- there are four or five varieties of
   DECtalk devices available.

   The following are for two common DECtalk devices: the
   DECtalk I (DTC01) and the DECtalk III (DTC03):

     EK-DTC01-OM-003    DECtalk Owner's Manual
     EK-DTC01-RM-003    DECtalk Programmer's Reference Manual
     EK-DTC01-IN-002    DECtalk Installation Guide
     EK-DTC01-RC-003    DECtalk Programmer's Reference Card
     EK-DTC01-PS        DTC01 Pocket Service Guide

     EK-DTC03-OM        DECtalk Owner's Manual
     EK-DTC03-IN        DECtalk Installation Guide
     EK-DTC03-PS        DECtalk Pocket Service Guide
     EK-DTC03-RC        DECtalk Programmer's Reference Card

     EY-6727E-TK        DECtalk Application Development Guide (TK50)
     EY-6727E-MT        DECtalk Application Development Guide(magtape)

   I don't happen to have the PC DECtalk (DTC07) documentation part
   numbers handy.  (These part numbers _should_ be listed in the
   installation guide.)

|>In particular, I need technical information about phonemes,
|>the callable C interface, and that sort of thing.

   The callable interface for the external DECtalk is the standard
   serial line I/O interface for the host operating system.  One sends
   ANSI escape sequences to the device.  Under OpenVMS, a second
   interface -- the DECtalk run-time library -- is also available.

   Phonemes are only documented in the DECtalk (and to some extent
   in the DECvoice) manuals.

   The OpenVMS DECtalk RTL is documented in the OpenVMS manual set,
   and is available on the online documentation CDROM.

   There is a DECtalk source library available on one of the DECUS
   tapes -- it was set up for use from C.

   Steve
-- 

