Yesterday, part of our network went away for a few minutes.  It was
rather interesting.  We have four segements bridged off the computer
room backbone.  Each bridge has an independent tap on the main
backbone.  Three of the bridges are in the same rack with the same
power distribution system.  There are 2 DECBridge 200s and one
DECBridge 90.  The DECbridge 90 tells us it has been up for more than
80 days; thus, we didn't lose power to the rack.  The only thing we
can figure is that the DECBridge 200s committed double suicide and
rebooted.  The whole network came back after about 5 minutes.

Has anyone seen problems like this with DECbridge 200s on a
multiprotocol network (DECnet, TCP-IP, LAT, IPX, FileNet)?

