Not I.  We've had a good number of LANbridge 200s installed for, oh,
7 years or so, with never any such problems.  (A fan went bad on one
once.)  They're real all-time workhorses.

There *was* a bug in the LANbridge microcode such that, if one
saw a packet with a source address of FF-FF-FF-FF-FF-FF, it would
"learn" that address and thence refuse to forward broadcasts.  But
that was fixed about 5 years ago.

I *wouldn't* be so sanguine about your DECbridge 90.

By the way, you can talk to your LANbridges if you have RBMS or 
ELMS (though God knows how you'd order them from DEC these days.)

