How to display custom characters with the following ASCII codes 
on a VMS DEC Terminal window?

 $A4, $A6, $AC, $AD, $AE, $AF, $B4, $B8, $BE, $D0, $DE, $F0, and $FE 

On a regular VT220, VT320 terminal it is possible to display these 
characters if defined in a soft character set.

I did the following to display custom characters on these positions
in a DEC terminal window:

-dumped the standard DECterm DECW$FONT to a BDF-file, using getbdf
-modified the character definitions from $A1 to $FE with xfed
-compiled the BDF-file using the FONT font compiler under VMS
-copied the resulting font to a directory in the font path and
 made it available (I can select and display the font with xfontsel)
-created a DEC terminal window with the appropriate resource settings
 for using this font.
-when dumping the font to the terminal I get my modified character set
 except the above listed characters. 

It seems as if the terminal programm masks these characters off.
Why does it do this? 
I know that these characters are not defined in the DEC Multinational 
Character Set GR Codes according to the "VT220 Programmer Pocket Guide",
but as mentioned above, on a regular VT terminal the redefinition and 
output of these characters works.

I am using Open VMS-V5.5-2H4 on an VAXstation 4000-90 with Motif 1.1.

Thanks for any help

      Uwe Illig
