  The 2100-series is a multiprocessor PCI system, and is supported by the
  OpenVMS, OSF/1 and NT operating systems.  The 2100 supports up to four
  CPUs, up to 2 GB memory, and up to 32 GB disk (inside the cabinet).  A
  CPU upgrade to the DECchip 21064A (275 MHz) is planned.

  2100-series ECC memory is available in 64 MB, 128 MB and 512 MB increments.
  Internal hardware RAID support is optional.

  The system bus in the 2100-series runs at 667 MB per second, the PCI
  at 132 MB per second, the EISA at 33 MB per second, and Ethernet peaks
  at about 1 MB per second.

  The current 2100-series Ethernet controller is the DE425-AA, an
  EISA controller. 

  I do not know what the current plans and/or schedules are for any PCI
  controllers.

