     ROBERT B. PALMER, PRESIDENT AND CEO, DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION
            TO DELIVER KEYNOTE ADDRESS AT DECUS '94/NEW ORLEANS



The U.S. Chapter of DECUS has announced that Robert B. Palmer, president
and CEO of Digital Equipment Corporation, will deliver the keynote address
at DECUS '94/New Orleans.

Mr. Palmer, who last addressed a DECUS U.S. Chapter audience a year ago, is
expected to update attendees on changes which have occurred at Digital as
well as provide insight to the company's future strategy and direction.

Mr. Palmer will deliver the keynote address during the event Welcoming
Session scheduled for May 9, at 8:30 A.M. in Ballroom 1 B/C, of the Ernest
N. Morial Convention Center, New Orleans, LA.

"I am very pleased that Bob has accepted our invitation to return and speak
with our attendees," said Chapter President Margaret Knox. "I believe that
his presence in New Orleans reinforces Digital's commitment to focus on the
customer, and serves to solidify DECUS as the premiere organization for
obtaining information on, and providing feedback to, Digital and related
vendors in the Digital marketplace."

Following the theme of "Managing Complexity: Succeeding in a Multivendor,
Multiplatform World", DECUS '94/New Orleans will focus on providing
Information Technology professionals with the information they need to
succeed in delivering services across multiplatform, multivendor
environments.

DECUS '94/New Orleans May 7-12, 1994, will feature in-depth seminars and
symposium sessions which cover virtually every area of computing, a hands-on
Digital Technology Center featuring the products, services, and technologies
of Digital Equipment Corporation, and the DECUS Trade Show where over 100
vendors from the Digital marketplace will showcase the latest applications
and software solution offerings.

Attendees are given the unique opportunity to interact, and learn from,
thousands of their technical peers, experienced product users, industry
leaders, and product engineers and developers.

For more information, or to register, contact DECUS Customer Service at
1-800-DECUS55.

The U.S. Chapter of DECUS, the Digital Equipment Computer Users Society, is
an association of Information Technology professionals interested in the
products, services, and technologies of Digital Equipment Corporation and
related vendors. The Association's purpose is to promote the unimpeded
exchange of information, with the goal of helping its members and their
organizations to be more successful. The Chapter provides members with means
to enhance their professional development, forums for technical training,
mechanisms for obtaining up-to-date information, advocacy programs, and
opportunities for informal disclosure and interaction with professional
colleagues of like interests.

