In article <1994Apr2.160829.2@mlvax.lonestar.org>,
 <marty@mlvax.lonestar.org> wrote:
>anybody know the pinouts of the 15 pin connector on this thing?

On the VS2000:

1: Red
2: RGB gnd
3: Mono gnd
4: +5V
5: TXD
6: earth
7: gnd
8: +12V
9: Mono
10: Green
11: Blue
12: -12V
13: RXD
14: KB
15: KB

The pins you want are 5, 13 and 7. I think you could use pins 14 and 15
somehow as well (since the keyboard is serial too), but I've never tried it.

Using pins 5, 13 and 7 works fine, and gives you tty01 if I'm not mistaken.

Good luck!

/tg



