  This is a  reminder about the two-part presentation by Digital Equipment
Canada and Kubota Pacific Computer on Thursday, April 14.

  The first part is titled "Digital's Technical Computing Strategy for the
90's". It will be a lecture and demonstration in Sanford Fleming, Room
1105, from 10:00 AM to 12:00 noon. 

  The second part consists of demonstrations and refreshments. These will
be available between 12:00 noon to 3:00 PM in the UTIRC Visualization and
Multimedia Laboratory at 4 Bancroft Avenue, Room 201

  Three of the major topics to be discussed are:
+ Kubota Pacific's Alpha-based high performance Denali 3D graphics
  subsystems,
+ DEC 2100 Series: Digital's high performance SMP UNIX Servers. This brand
  new, low cost system was announced on April 12. A demonstration system
  will be available.
+ Parallel Compiler Technology (DEC Fortran-90 with HPF). This part of the
  presentation will be given by David Loveman, Senior Program Manager at
  Digital Equipment Corporation in the areas of programming language
  strategies, compiler architectures, and parallel computing. He is
  Digital's representative to the High Performance Fortran Forum, is
  co-author of the recently published book "The High Performance Fortran
  Handbook".

  Other topics to be covered include DEC's Alpha AXP workstation clusters,
Gigaswitch NETWORK technology (3.6 Gbits/s, 22 FDDI ports), and Digital's
new Parallel Development Environment (PSE).

