>I have recently gotten an LK401 key board, which unlike my old Dec
keyboard.
>
>This key board has a left and right compose character keys,
>and right and left alt function keys.
> 
>The left compose character key continues to behave as the it did on
>my old keyboard: as a meta key.
>
>However, I can't figure out how to remap the remaining new keys.  They
>appear to be no ops, and even using xev and striking them gets me
nothing.
>
>Anyone know how to deal with this?
>
  The LK401 powers up in LK201 compatability mode, and must be put into
  LK401 mode to obtain the other key values.  Both OpenVMS and OSF
  (and Ultrix) handle this correctly.  Setting up the keyboard can be
  a little tricky, since the LK401 is a little more picky about when
  you can send it commands than the LK201 (for instance, you can't
  send it a command while it's transmitting a power up sequence).
  

