I found this information in the Software Product Description
(a printed copy of which should have been shipped with your
system software; you can also get it via the WWW as
	http://www.dec.com/pub/Digital/info/SPD/41-61-05.txt):

 Software Documentation:
    Full Documentation Kit: QA-MT4AA-GZ

 The full documentation kit contains the following:
    End User Documentation: QA-MT4AB-GZ
    Developer's Documentation for DEC OSF/1 Developers' Toolkit and DEC
    OSF/1 C Developers' Extensions: QA-MT5AA-GZ

    Server Documentation for DEC OSF/1 Server Extensions: QA-MT6AA-GZ

 Note: The Technical Overview document (Order Number: AA-QOR1A-TE) is
 included in the End User Documentation Set.

If you don't want to order the full doc kit, the part number for
the "Guide to System Administration" (OSF/1 V2.0) is AA-PS2RB-TE.

>Can someone from DEC explain to me why your sales reps. are
>asking me for DEC part numbers?

This is not an "official explanation", but I don't know an easy
way of getting part numbers for such documents unless you already
have the doc kit (I went to our bookshelf to find the guide and
its part number).

All OSF/1 documents are listed in the "Documentation Overview",
part no. AA-PS2JB-TE, on page 28 or so.

According to the "Documentation Overview", you can get help
with documentation orders by calling 1-800-DIGITAL and asking
for Technical Support.  If that doesn't work, your sales person
should be encouraged to ask his or her sales support staff, who
should have a copy of the document, or the Customer Support Center.  

-Jeff

P.S.: To complicate things further, if you want to save money and
shelf space, you might want to get the documentation on CD-ROM.
I didn't bother to find the part number for that.


