This news group has been kind enough to help me out with a sticky
problem concerning OSF/1 documentation, so I just thought I would
summarize what I have learned to try to help others that may be
stuck with a similar problem.  Here was my original problem:  About
24 hrs ago I started to add a new disk drive to my DEC Alpha workstation.
I check the man pages on the doconfig command, and it said something
to the effect:  If you get into trouble, look in the "Guide to System
Administration".  Since I did not have this document I started calling
all the people I knew at DEC and none of them knew how I could obtain
a copy of this document.  I then posted this question on the net
and found out the following:

DEC has switched over to on-line documentation distrubuted on a CD that
usually comes with the computer.  Unfortunately I did not receive this CD
with my computer (I guess this is because I bought a demo machine.  In 
fairness to DEC, they gave me a great price on the machine, but they
did not ship me most of the accessories that normally come with DEC
workstations, including things like the operating system and documentaiton
CDs)

The manual that I originally inquired about is apparently available on
the CD.  Now the next catch, the document in in "Bookreader" format.
It appears that there is no way to print out a document using the
Bookreader software.  This means that this is ONLY available on-line.
This works great if your computer is up and running, but I am not sure
what you are supposed to do if you need the document that has the 
instructions on how to boot your computer if things don't work right
(which is what got me started in this whole mess to start with).

