Lots of people.

Digital, in their wisdom, decided that since DECnet does not use broadcasts
(and VAXen run only DECnet), they could reduce interrupt load by having the
DEBNA treat broadcast as just another multicast address. You must program the
interface to see broadcasts. Most (all?) third party IP implementations take
care of this.

