No, you don't have to set the unit numbers to the connector numbers. The RA81
unit number is set using the unit plugs on the front of the drives. (Those
are the oblong, white plugs.) Look at the 'pins' on the plug. How the pins are
REMoved sets the 'number' of the plug. It should be binary (1,2,4,8,16,etc.)
Just don't use the same unit number as your other drives on that controller.
